Hi Gabriele,

Thanks for getting back so quickly 🙏  


* Are referred drivers aware their personal info will be shown to referrers? If not, why not? {color:#ff5630}They are not aware, though most of the time they share their details with whoever refer them. With scouts they even share all their details and docs so the scout can help them sign up. However this is something we can add in our referral comms email the registered driver gets when they sign up using a referral code (see below). Please note today their details are not visible in the app, only when we share manual reports with Scouts.{color}
!Screenshot 2025-06-11 at 17.24.35.png|width=596,height=769,alt="Screenshot 2025-06-11 at 17.24.35.png"!
* Is there a cap on how long or how much of this data is visible? {color:#ff5630}Currently it seems like referrals stay on for 75 days in the app even after completion or expiration. I can check with Product if we can reduce this time and by how much. Additionally for personal data, we should remove the phone number and the number of trips once their friend achieve their targets or the campaign has expired, so the referrer can no longer contact them.{color} {color:#ff5630}Would that work?{color}
* Are there any abuse prevention controls, like throttling outreach or flagging harassment? {color:#ff5630}We don’t have those in place as contacts happen offline outside our platform. So far with scouts we haven’t had any complaint from drivers as they’ve been benefiting from their support. Do you have any recommendation we could implement?{color}
* Could we show progress without identity info to meet the same goal? Or, alternatively, can we show less data? {color:#ff5630}We could show only the first name instead of full name. We can also only show the phone number instead of both phone and email.  {color}
* Am I correct to understand that we want to, ideally, upload this DSA online where the DSA would be easy to reach? If yes, we can do it, but would it be possible to introduce a checkbox somewhere? {color:#ff5630}Not really, I wanted to see if there was an alternative to the DSA where we can integrate the agreement with the app T&Cs? What could work best in this case without adding manual work or separate agreement flows?{color}
* Has this been run past Product Legal? {color:#ff5630}Not yet, I thought this was a Privacy topic so only reached out here. Happy to create a ticket for Product Legal too - let me know.{color}
* Which countries will we launch this in? {color:#ff5630}This will be launched in all countries{color}



I didn’t share in the ticket but this feature is not yet live, we are just starting the design of the feature and engineering development is planned for Q3. We require Privacy input to finalise the feature design.

Hi all - just chipping in some thoughts from the privacy side:

{quote}_Should we use the same email inbox as for Bolt Link to communicate with agency drivers?_{quote}

* Fine from a Privacy POV. Usual advice applies when sending direct marketing communications (e.g., must have an unsubscribe option).

{quote}_Can we use previously approved comms for bolt link drivers?_{quote}

* *General*: Terminology / factual accuracy will need to be updated where applicable for agency drivers.
* *Prospective Driver Bs*: I would update the disclaimer language to the following (and tweak the square brackets as applicable:”_“Bolt has collected your contact information from another driver for the purpose of (per that driver’s request) inviting you to act as their substitute. Bolt processes your contact information based on its legitimate interest in allowing drivers to create a list of substitutes (thereby ensuring that the services provided by drivers are flexible). If you do not accept this invitation, Bolt will delete your contact information after [a reasonable period / 30 days]. For further information on how Bolt processes personal data, please refer to Bolt’s privacy notices.”_

{quote}_When placing blocks for drivers Bs (bolt link) due to incorrect or expired documents, can we contact driver B regarding the reasons for the block, or should this communication only go through the fleet owner? Is it acceptable for them to receive automated notifications?_{quote}

* Is this block a fully automated process? Does it differ in any way to the process currently in place for principal model drivers who have expired documents?
* If we do not contact Driver B directly, how will they be informed about the block / the reasoning behind it? Will this be sent by Driver A, or not at all? We should aim to find some way for this information to reach Driver B, as otherwise they will claim we are not being transparent about any applicable suspensions.

{quote}_E.g. when a driver uploads documents under their principal profile and we duplicate it under their driver B account - is it necessary to get driver A’s explicit approval or is a notification sufficient?_{quote}

* Driver A’s consent should not be needed from a privacy POV. Notification should be sufficient.

{quote}_When a driver B submits a car application, should we only change it on the driver B profile or duplicate across all profiles if the currently used vehicle matches across profiles?_{quote}

* Agreed with Ieva’s point. However, no strong preferences either way from a strictly privacy POV.

