*Reason for being rejected*
The OpenAPI spec is meant to describe the public API surface (endpoints, request/response schemas). In this case, the `UserRefundActorAtFault` is not directly utilised by any endpoint, so it has been excluded. Only one value from the `UserRefundActionAtFault` enum is used, but this will not prompt the generation of the entire enum. Instead, the openapi-generator will only include the specific value needed, which is the provider value in this instance.

{noformat}// spec
"DeliveryProviderPortal.ProviderDeduction": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "actor_at_fault": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "provider"
            ]
          },
          "amount": {
            "type": "number"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "actor_at_fault",
          "amount"
        ]
      }{noformat}

{noformat}//Generated code
export interface ProviderDeduction {
    actor_at_fault: 'provider';
    amount: number;
}{noformat}



If there is a need for this enum to be used, it has to be fully referenced in a schema that is used by an endpoint.

