Dear Костянтин,

We are writing further to your previous response, dated 22 May 2025.

We note that your request focuses on the restriction of access to your Bolt driver account. As noted in previous correspondence, this was the result of *failed Identification verification.* Bolt requires drivers to successfully complete identity verification in accordance with platform security standards and applicable regulations. This verification process is essential to ensure that only authorized individuals operate under valid driver profiles. In your case, the verification attempt did not meet the required criteria {color:#ff5630}*[in particular,* {color}{color:#ff5630}*_explanation of face not matching_*{color}{color:#ff5630}*]*{color}, and as a result, access to your account was restricted to prevent potential misuse or unauthorized access. {color:#ff5630}*_[Please note that our specialist team are currently reviewing the restriction of access to your account and we will revert with an update in this regard.]_*{color}

Bolt uses automated processes for the purposes of detecting and preventing fraud (and applying suspensions and blocks, including restricting access to accounts, as needed). However, such processes either: (a) rely on relevant exceptions under applicable data protection laws and regulations; (b) do not produce legal or similarly significant effects on individuals; or (c) are subject to human review. Please note that Bolt is unable to provide the names of Bolt employees that review any decisions to restrict access of Bolt driver accounts, as this comprises their personal data and disclosure would violate their rights and freedoms.

For information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Policy at [https://bolt.eu/uk-ua/privacy/|https://bolt.eu/uk-ua/privacy/] , which includes further information about:

* The categories of personal data we process;
* The purposes for which we process personal data;
* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;
* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;
* The sources of personal data received from other parties;
* Your rights in relation to your personal data;
* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making/profiling of personal data; and
* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.

If you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy. If you have any additional questions, please let us know.

Yours sincerely, 

*Bolt*

